-   **What is not covered?** The speaker, the slides and anything outside our own inventory.

## What a Keynote Speaker Usually Asks For

A speaker's rider is a short list, and it repeats from one event to the next. The usual items are:

-   **A microphone.** A handheld, a clip on lavalier or an over the ear headset, depending on whether the speaker moves and gestures.
-   **A lectern or a stage space.** Some speakers want a lectern for notes. Others prefer to walk and want a clear floor.
-   **A screen and a projector or a display.** For the slides, and sometimes a video with sound.
-   **A way to connect their laptop.** Most bring their own and need the right cable.
-   **A stage monitor.** A speaker facing the audience cannot hear the speakers pointed at the audience, so a monitor lets them hear themselves.
-   **A sound check.** A short test of the microphone and the levels before the audience arrives.

## Which Microphone Suits the Speaker

The microphone is the item the speaker cares about most, and the choice depends on how they speak.

-   **A speaker who stays at a lectern** uses a gooseneck microphone. Our [lectern rental guide](/blog/lectern-rental/) explains the lectern and the gooseneck that goes on it.
-   **A speaker who walks the stage** is better served by a handheld, or by a hands free microphone if they gesture. We own six wireless handheld microphones, all Audix, and our [guide to wireless handheld microphone rental](/blog/wireless-handheld-microphone-rental/) explains which package carries one.
-   **A speaker who needs both hands free**, to use a clicker or to demonstrate something, wants a lavalier or a headset. We own wireless lavalier sets and a headband microphone, as a separate item that none of our packages includes. Our [headset and lavalier microphone guide](/blog/headset-lavalier-microphone-rental/) compares the two.

The speaker's rider often names the type. If it does not, ask the speaker, because a change on the day costs time that the schedule does not have.

## Lectern, Screen and Slides

If the speaker wants a lectern, the MICE Pack lists a methacrylate one as an optional extra at 50 euros. We own two. The gooseneck microphone goes on top.

For the slides, the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a 60 inch LED display, and the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) includes a 5000 lumen projector with a screen and one premium wireless handheld microphone, at 310 euros ex VAT. For connecting a laptop, that pack lists the adapters we provide for HDMI and USB-C and the audio interfaces.

The speaker runs their own slides. Our technician operates the sound and the microphones, so the speaker or someone from the speaker's team controls what is shown. Have the presentation on the laptop and a copy on a USB drive, in case the laptop fails.

